Z||000004||BAM-BAM||06-19-2000||04:14 PM||||  Haze, Pictures won't be back for a few days. I had them developed by KODAK onto CD. But, the spoiler is well worth the money. It looks fantastic. There is one little problem that I am working on; it doesn't use gaskets so I have to make some. There is a slight lift on the inside of the mounting surface due to the contour of the Mustang deck. It's about 1/8" and requires some type of gasket to fill the void. The spoiler is very rigid, therefore no flex. It's been an idea that I wanted to try for quite a while and finally got the opportunity to do it. I got my spoiler on E-Bay as well from a guy named Cale Beck, he's very easy to deal with. I understand your apprehension and if you want to wait for the pics I'm sure there will be others on E-Bay, there always are. But believe me, it's awesome. I even had a Corvette guy give it a second look and a thumbs up this morning. It's still painted white and will be untill I get to the paint phase if my project, but it still looks like it belongs there. If you like the way I mounted it (towards the rear), I'll give you detailed instruction on how I layed it out. It was pretty simple really. Changes the whole profile of the car and will look good with one of TOM's Scoops(coming soon). Well, that's enough for now. Let me know what you decide to do.<P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
