Z||000007||BAM-BAM||06-19-2000||05:40 PM||||  Haze, I got my spoiler for $53.00+ shipping, pretty good deal. Yeah he took his time, about three weeks. I called him on the phone and he explained why it took so long. He works for some aerosomething company during the day and does custom Mustang mods in his spare time. His shop is twenty or so miles from his house in one direction and UPS is thirty miles away in the other. His computor is at his shop thereby explaining his inability, at times, to provide a prompt response. And he only goes to the UPS office once a week due to travel constraints. He gave me the tracking number so that I could watch the spoiler on it's journey. I would'nt hesitate to buy from him again if he had something that I needed. I would certainly try to be more patient. I bugged the hell out of the guy. But all is good again and I am happy with the spoiler.       Brocar, I assume by your screen name that you have an 87 Fiero? GT, SE, or coupe? That's a pretty radical spoiler design you are looking at. Why don't you wait till I post some pics and see what you think. I have and 85GT notchback, but I would bet this spoiler would look even better on a Fastback GT. Just so you all know I'm not the type to over mod something especially when it comes to appearance. My other body mods will be ZR2 hood, Earne's Mecham style side intakes, Tom's rear deck scoop, and that little drop spoiler that fits under the aeronose. I think it's called a chin spoiler? Anyway, These are all muscle mods to give that "Phat" fat appearance. Well that's about all I have untill the pics get back. Hope you all aren't dissapointed.<P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||6
